{"id": "EUVD-2026-56977", "enisaUuid": "3a032c46-17e8-36a9-92ad-0db254400c34", "description": "A flaw was found in FreeIPA. The trust-fetch-domains command is gated by a read-only permission on the trust object rather than a trust-administration permission, allowing an authenticated, non-privileged IPA user to trigger a privileged Active Directory trust refresh using an attacker-supplied server and credentials, resulting in unauthorized, attacker-controlled modification of trusted-domain and ID-range identity data in the IPA LDAP directory.", "datePublished": "2026-08-11T20:46:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T05:07:56", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:70564", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:72279", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:82935", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83083", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83084", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83085", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83460", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:83461", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-19550", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2514019"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6xg7-8fr6-8p33", "CVE-2026-19550"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1734b556-ce7a-3550-b8df-61580cad8442", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:4.13.4-1.el9_8"}, {"id": "1cb41c46-cda2-3722-92b9-07ec60e63cc0", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 8100020261007071200.143e9e98"}, {"id": "475128aa-ac9b-3bd7-b8ff-39ef8e17405a", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.4 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:4.11.0-15.el9_4.9"}, {"id": "559b5457-5fb0-36cc-a0